# Next.js and React

## Next.js 16

This project uses Next.js 16 with breaking changes vs older versions. When unsure, read guides under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and follow deprecation notices in `AGENTS.md`.

## App Router

- Use App Router conventions (`app/` directory).
- Default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only when needed (forms, hooks, browser APIs).
- API: Route Handlers in `app/api/**/route.ts`.

## Code style

- Functional components only.
- Import via `@/*` path alias (see `tsconfig.json`).
- Styling: Tailwind CSS 4 only — no Material UI, Bootstrap, or other heavy UI kits.
- Colocate feature UI under `components/`; avoid bloating `app/page.tsx`.

## UX expectations (from AC)

- Responsive layout, accessible labels, loading state on submit, disabled submit when invalid.
- Success and error feedback visible to the user.

Verify UI work against `docs/ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md` §1, §2, and §10 (frontend features).
